# A PreToolUse hook (testdata/behaviour/qa/hook-blocks-bash/.claude/
# settings.json) blocks a bash call before it runs. GuardToolCall
# (internal/claude/hooks/runner.go) treats the hook's exit 2 as a block,
# whose stderr becomes the Reason; internal/harness/turn.go ~658 turns
# that Reason into the tool's own isError result content verbatim (no
# "blocked by hook:" prefix - that prefix is app.go's separate
# UserPromptSubmit-hook path, not this PreToolUse one), so it commits as
# an ordinary red Bash CallError block carrying the hook's message.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-hook-blocks-tool.yaml
@fixture testdata/behaviour/qa/hook-blocks-bash

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE run the blocked command
SHOT typed
KEY enter
WAITFOR /blocked: bash is disabled for this scenario/ 20
SHOT blocked
EXPECT /blocked: bash is disabled for this scenario/
EXPECT /bash ─/
WAITFOR /Noted, the call was blocked/ 10
SHOT reply
EXPECT_NOT /blocked by hook:/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
